    "q-134181": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134181",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "It takes $7$ hours for a snail to crawl $210$ centimeters, moving at a constant pace. Find the distance this snail covers in $4$ hours.",
      "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in centimeters per hour, we divide the number of centimeters $210,$ by the number of hours, $7.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{210}{7} & =210÷7 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the snail is $30$ centimeters per hour. \n\nTo find the distance covered in $4$ hours, we multiply the speed by $4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\times \\text{time} \\\\  & =30\\times 4 \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the snail covers $120$ centimeters in $4$ hours.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
