    "q-134223": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134223",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "An arrow takes $3$ seconds to travel $360$ meters at a constant pace. How long does it take for the arrow to travel $660$ meters?",
      "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in meters per second, we divide the number of meters, which is $360,$ by the number of seconds, $3.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{360}{3} & =360÷3 \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the arrow is $120$ meters per second. \n\nTo find the time it takes the arrow to cover $660$ meters, we divide the distance by $120.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{660}{120} \\\\  & =\\frac{660÷60}{120÷60} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2} \\\\  & =11÷2 \\\\  & =5.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the arrow $5.5$ seconds to travel $660$ meters.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
