    "q-134004": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134004",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "It takes $20$ minutes for a slug to crawl $90$ centimeters at a constant pace. How much time does it take for the slug to crawl $450$ centimeters?",
      "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in centimeters per minute, we divide the number of centimeters, which is $90,$ by the number of minutes, $20.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{90}{20} & =\\frac{90÷10}{20÷10} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =9÷2 \\\\  & =4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the slug is $4.5$ centimeters per minute. \n\nTo find the time it took the slug to cover $450$ centimeters, we divide the distance by $4.5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{450}{4.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{450\\cdot 10}{4.5\\cdot 10} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\,500}{45} \\\\  & =\\frac{45\\cdot 100}{45} \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the slug $100$ minutes to crawl $450$ centimeters.",
